{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>That we acted foolishly.</b> Against you. <b>And that we sinned.</b> Against the Shekhinah. And the sense of the word נואלנו is that speech in that matter was folly to the one speaking it." "<b>And in tractate</b> Zevaḥim, chapter Tevul Yom, they said: Miriam — who confined her? If you say Moses, he was a זר (non-priest), and a זר does not inspect the nega'im (skin afflictions); and if you say Aaron, he was a close relative, and a close relative does not inspect the nega'im. Rather, the Holy One, blessed be He, apportioned honor to Miriam at that hour: He said, 'I am a priest — I confine her, I declare her impure, and I release her.'"], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:31:52.643377306Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}